{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03RY", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a9079b8635d17eee3fc254abb8d798bca4188851e37bcadd5f195e7739fd323", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the following lemma we use a standard trick to reduce a very general\nstatement to the Noetherian case.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f5848d8cbc5c641d458cc663c861e362886553c75e1030c94ba281be16fd359e", "unit_id": "tag:03RY:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03RY", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[Exposee IX, Proposition 2.14]{SGA4}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow\n\\prod\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} f_{i, *}\\underline{E_i}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$f_i : Y_i \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$E_i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} f_{i, *}\\underline{M_i}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$f_i : Y_i \\to X$", "MATH_0011": "$M_i$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0015": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0016": "$$\n\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} f_{i, *}\\underline{M_i}\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$f_i : Y_i \\to X$", "MATH_0018": "$M_i$", "MATH_0019": "$\\Lambda$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-constructible-maps-into-constant-general}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e403a081ecbbb8d1ab106e41602f3c76600246baec005bb23f9d0b9233fde250", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0e24dbaaa3244a37f68e23425c6a4c17c398e8805a4b3b145497007d87bcb6dd", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Let <MATH_0002> be a constructible sheaf of sets on <MATH_0003>.\nThere exist an injective map of sheaves\n<MATH_0004>\nwhere <MATH_0005> is a finite and finitely presented morphism and\n<MATH_0006> is a finite set.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0007> be a constructible abelian sheaf on <MATH_0008>.\nThere exist an injective map of abelian sheaves\n<MATH_0009>\nwhere <MATH_0010> is a finite and finitely presented morphism and\n<MATH_0011> is a finite abelian group.\n<STRUCT_0004> Let <MATH_0012> be a Noetherian ring.\nLet <MATH_0013> be a constructible sheaf of <MATH_0014>-modules on <MATH_0015>.\nThere exist an injective map of sheaves of modules\n<MATH_0016>\nwhere <MATH_0017> is a finite and finitely presented morphism and\n<MATH_0018> is a finite <MATH_0019>-module.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:747059d288be1ea517974d6ae592192fd5e8f62c4b1d33b824ddebb01a4d14b4", "unit_id": "tag:09Z7:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "math_text_regions": [{"delimiter_kind": "display-dollar", "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "region_id": "math/0001", "slots": [{"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "sites.tex", "kind": "section", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 316727, "start": 316718}, "command_hash": "sha256:3ddb92ccb3118de03d8d58e0e2b9a68498744d79e806286109a3f511be1cd231", "container_byte_span": {"end": 317111, "start": 315098}, "container_hash": "sha256:c301cf74a2dd2305f3d1af83a4e72e18582d3c42daab021c29963eac16107da4"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "sites-section-2-category", "owner_tag": "04I9", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:6648093c080d9362cea0de2507eb65d250f9c12f8a00a7e5b534320688290537", "source_label": "sites-section-2-category", "usage": "quad-connector", "usage_source": {"after": "\\quad", "before": "\\quad", "environments": []}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "sites-or", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 104, "start": 102}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": "or"}], "source": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}_t \\longrightarrow\n\\prod\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} f_{i, *}\\underline{E_i}\n\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\n\\mathcal{F}_t \\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} f_{i, *}\\underline{M_i}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 946, "start": 741}, "source_hash": "sha256:a64ce20f2462480a1daa30ec7f774edf9fe15f7c0a05cc70637a8eeba0f70aa3"}], "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03RY", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}_t \\longrightarrow\n\\prod\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} f_{i, *}\\underline{E_i}\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n\\mathcal{F}_t \\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} f_{i, *}\\underline{M_i}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$X = \\lim_{t \\in T} X_t$", "MATH_0002": "$X_t$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0005": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$X_t$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}_t$", "MATH_0009": "$X_t$", "MATH_0010": "$t$", "MATH_0011": "$X_t$", "MATH_0012": "$f_i : Y_i \\to X_t$", "MATH_0013": "$X_t$", "MATH_0014": "$f_i$", "MATH_0015": "$f_{i, *}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{limits-proposition-approximate}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-category-is-colimit}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-constructible-maps-into-constant}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-finite-pushforward-commutes-with-base-change}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:93e2ba13ea7756ee5c3439dd383659af411f514b96a5fcc28ec52c7dd164b8a9", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:6f00f2754e2cb989293355a0484c6dc9733fd563f539acbd085503ba4697fa40", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd8e6b69040810bdb885fbc1b367e2fa404f9eadbc9d80c9e72be3f22380ffd7", "source_text": "We will reduce this lemma to the Noetherian case by absolute Noetherian\napproximation. Namely, by\nLimits, Proposition <REF_0001>\nwe can write <MATH_0001> with each <MATH_0002> of finite type over\n<MATH_0003> and with affine transition morphisms. By\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthe category of constructible sheaves (of sets, abelian groups, or\n<MATH_0004>-modules) on <MATH_0005> is the colimit of the corresponding\ncategories for <MATH_0006>. Thus our constructible sheaf <MATH_0007>\nis the pullback of a similar constructible sheaf <MATH_0008>\nover <MATH_0009> for some <MATH_0010>. Then we apply the Noetherian case\n(Lemma <REF_0003>)\nto find an injection\n<MATHSEG_0001>or<MATHSEG_0002>\nover <MATH_0011> for some finite morphisms <MATH_0012>.\nSince <MATH_0013> is Noetherian the morphisms <MATH_0014> are of finite presentation.\nSince pullback is exact and since formation of <MATH_0015> commutes\nwith base change\n(Lemma <REF_0004>), we conclude.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bcf06f2744b1241fdd1de568182abc21fa1acc9bf08666775cd72b9124fb80b5", "unit_id": "tag:09Z7:proof"}
